title: Example - Markdown code block - longer fences
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Markdown

The opening run's length pins the minimum close. With a 4-backtick open, the body can contain 3-backtick runs without terminating early — useful when the code block is itself markdown documenting other code blocks.

Live:

````md
Markdown fenced block syntax:

```js
const x = 1;
```
````

Source (5-tick to enclose):

`````
````md
Markdown fenced block syntax:

```js
const x = 1;
```
````
`````

The 4-tick open looks for a 4-or-more-tick close on its own line; the inner 3-tick runs are body text.

